    "title": "Moton School Campus in Taft added to National Register of Historic Places - NewsBreak",
    "text": "news9.com\nwebsite\nTaft\nMoton School Campus in Taft added to National Register of Historic Places\n3 hours ago\nThe Moton School Campus Historic District in Taft has officially been added to the National Register of Historic Places. The original Moton School was built in 1949 to educate Black children during the Jim Crow era, offering opportunity and hope to generations of students. Though the original building burned down in the 1960s, the site is now home to Taft’s City Hall and community center, still a central gathering place for the town.",
